# Style guide is mandatory

Read `.cursor/rules/style-guide.md` before writing or editing code. Follow every rule in that file.

A feature, fix, refactor, or any code change is **not done** until every changed file complies with that guide.

After implementation, re-read **all** changed files and verify:

- Explicit named intermediate values (do not nest meaningful method calls)
- One logical operation per statement
- One chained method per line; continuation indent is primary structure + 4 spaces (extra tab when hierarchy is weak)
- No PHP ternary operators
- Arrays and multiline arguments indented per the guide
- Sequential, readable flow; no clever shortcuts
- KISS (`.cursor/rules/kiss.mdc`): simplest solution that meets the requirement; no overengineering

If any file fails this review, keep working. Tests and Pint passing is not enough.

Do not treat Pint or PSR-12 as a substitute. This project’s style guide is stricter.
